---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro'
import { hospital } from '../data/site'
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  subtitle="How we collect, use, share and protect your personal data under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023."
  updated="September 2026"
>
  <h2>1. Overview</h2>
  <p>
    {hospital.name} ("we", "our", "us") respects your privacy and is committed to protecting your personal data.
    This policy explains what data we collect through this website ({hospital.domains.primary} and
    {hospital.domains.secondary}), why we collect it, how we use and safeguard it, how long we keep it, and the
    rights you have as a Data Principal.
  </p>
  <p>
    We process personal data in accordance with the <strong>Digital Personal Data Protection Act, 2023 (DPDP Act)</strong>,
    the rules made under it, and other applicable Indian law. By using this website you confirm that you have read and
    understood this notice.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Data We Collect</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact and identity data:</strong> name, phone number, email address, age, gender and city that you submit through appointment booking, camp registration, the contact form or newsletter subscription.</li>
    <li><strong>Health information you choose to share:</strong> the symptoms, conditions or reason for visit you voluntarily enter in a booking or enquiry form. We request only what is needed to arrange your care.</li>
    <li><strong>Communication data:</strong> the content of messages you send to us and our replies.</li>
    <li><strong>Technical data:</strong> IP address, browser type, device type, pages visited and referral source, collected in aggregated form for security and service improvement.</li>
    <li><strong>Preferences:</strong> essential cookies and local storage used to remember your light/dark mode choice.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Purpose and Legal Basis for Processing</h2>
  <p>
    We process your personal data on the basis of your <strong>consent</strong> (which you give by submitting a form and can
    withdraw at any time) and, where applicable, for a <strong>legitimate use</strong> such as providing health services you
    request, responding to a medical emergency, or meeting legal obligations. We use your data only to:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Schedule, confirm and manage appointments and camp registrations.</li>
    <li>Respond to your enquiries and provide the information or service you asked for.</li>
    <li>Send appointment confirmations, reminders and service updates related to your request.</li>
    <li>Send the health newsletter, only where you have opted in.</li>
    <li>Maintain the security and integrity of this website.</li>
    <li>Comply with applicable legal, accounting, accreditation and regulatory requirements.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Health Information</h2>
  <p>
    Health information you share through this website is treated with the strictest confidentiality and is used only for
    the purpose for which you provided it. This website does not create a formal medical record. Clinical records created
    during an in-person or teleconsultation visit are governed by hospital policy, the Indian Medical Council (Professional
    Conduct, Etiquette and Ethics) Regulations and applicable law, and are retained as required for patient care and by statute.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Third-Party Data Processors</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell your personal data. We may share limited data with service providers who process it on our behalf under
    written confidentiality and data-processing obligations, strictly to operate this website and communicate with you.
    These categories include:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>Email / SMS delivery providers used to send appointment confirmations and notifications.</li>
    <li>Cloud hosting and infrastructure providers that store the website and its database.</li>
    <li>Payment gateway providers, where you choose to make an online payment.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Where data is transferred or processed outside India, we take reasonable contractual steps to ensure a comparable
    standard of protection, subject to any restrictions notified by the Government of India.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Retention of Data</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Enquiries, appointments and camp registrations:</strong> retained for up to <strong>24 months</strong> from the date of submission, then securely deleted or anonymised.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter subscriptions:</strong> retained until you unsubscribe, and then for a short suppression period to honour your opt-out.</li>
    <li><strong>Clinical and billing records:</strong> retained for the period required by applicable medical, accreditation and tax law.</li>
    <li><strong>Server and security logs:</strong> retained for a limited period for security and audit purposes.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Your Rights as a Data Principal</h2>
  <p>Subject to applicable law, you have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Access</strong> a summary of the personal data we hold about you and how it is processed.</li>
    <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate, incomplete or outdated data.</li>
    <li><strong>Erase</strong> data that is no longer necessary for the purpose for which it was collected.</li>
    <li><strong>Withdraw consent</strong> at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of prior processing.</li>
    <li><strong>Nominate</strong> another individual to exercise your rights in the event of your death or incapacity.</li>
    <li><strong>Grievance redressal</strong> — raise a complaint with our Grievance Officer (below).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact our Data Protection / Grievance Officer:</p>
  <p>
    <strong>Grievance Officer — {hospital.name}</strong><br />
    {hospital.address.line1}, {hospital.address.line2}, {hospital.address.city}, {hospital.address.state} — {hospital.address.pincode}<br />
    Email: {hospital.email}<br />
    Phone: {hospital.phones.reception}
  </p>
  <p>We will acknowledge your request promptly and aim to resolve it within <strong>30 days</strong>.</p>

  <h2>8. Children's Data</h2>
  <p>
    This website is not directed at children. We do not knowingly collect or process the personal data of anyone under
    <strong>18 years of age</strong> without verifiable consent from a parent or lawful guardian. Where a minor requires an
    appointment, the booking must be made by a parent or guardian. If you believe a minor has provided us data without such
    consent, please contact us and we will delete it.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Data Security</h2>
  <p>
    We apply reasonable technical and organisational safeguards — including encryption in transit where supported, access
    controls, and encrypted storage of sensitive configuration — to protect your data against loss, misuse and unauthorised
    access. No internet transmission is completely secure, so please avoid sharing highly sensitive information through
    website forms when a phone call would suffice.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Cookies and Local Storage</h2>
  <p>
    We use only essential cookies and local storage required for core functionality such as your theme preference. We do not
    use advertising or cross-site tracking cookies. You can clear or block cookies in your browser, though some preferences
    may not be retained.
  </p>

  <h2>11. External Links</h2>
  <p>
    This website links to external services such as maps and social media. We are not responsible for their privacy
    practices. Please review their policies separately.
  </p>

  <h2>12. Changes to This Policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy to reflect changes in law or our practices. The "last updated" date at the top of this page
    reflects the most recent revision, and material changes will be highlighted on the website.
  </p>

  <h2>13. Contact</h2>
  <p>
    For questions about this policy or how your data is handled, write to <strong>{hospital.email}</strong> or contact the
    Grievance Officer details above.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
